.TH ARENA-SETUP 1 "July 2026" "UCI Arena Manager" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
arena-setup \- inspect, install, repair, upgrade, and remove UCI Arena components
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B arena-setup
[\fICOMMON OPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fICOMMAND OPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B arena-setup
is the typed, noninteractive-capable lifecycle client used by the platform
installers. It verifies signed catalogs and component payloads, maintains
receipts, and invokes only declared provider lifecycle entrypoints.
.PP
For ordinary desktop setup, use the reviewed install actions inside UCI Arena
Manager, the Windows installer Modify action, or the distribution package
workflow. Direct use is intended for automation and advanced administration.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-catalog " " \fIPATH\fR
Use the exact catalog at
.IR PATH .
.TP
.BR \-\-install-root " " \fIPATH\fR
Override the immutable component installation root.
.TP
.BR \-\-data-root " " \fIPATH\fR
Override the persistent Manager data and receipt root.
.TP
.BR \-\-cache-root " " \fIPATH\fR
Override the verified download cache.
.TP
.BR \-\-workspace-root " " \fIPATH\fR
Override the provider workspace root.
.TP
.BR \-\-knowledge-root " " \fIPATH\fR
Override the opening-book and tablebase activation root.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine-readable JSON.
.TP
.BR \-\-result-file " " \fIPATH\fR
Write the final machine-readable result to the native desktop helper's private
one-use result path. This option is for the authenticated desktop setup bridge;
ordinary CLI use should read standard output.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B inventory
Report installed, retained, detected, and missing resources.
.TP
.B plan
Resolve a preset or explicit component selection without changing the host.
.TP
.B apply
Apply a confirmed installation plan.
.TP
.B verify
Verify receipts, immutable payloads, generated configuration, and lifecycle
state.
.TP
.B repair
Restage and reverify selected components.
.TP
.B upgrade
Apply the selected components from a newer verified catalog.
.TP
.B uninstall
Remove selected managed component authority while preserving documented
operator data.
.SH COMMON COMMAND OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-preset " " \fINAME\fR
Select
.BR complete_arena ,
.BR manager_only ,
or
.BR custom .
.TP
.BR \-\-component " " \fIID\fR
Select an exact component ID. May be repeated where supported.
.TP
.B \-\-offline
Require all bytes to come from retained verified media.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Confirm a mutating operation noninteractively.
.TP
.B \-\-download-missing-knowledge
Select the bounded default opening-book and tablebase components.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
arena-setup --json inventory
arena-setup --json plan --preset complete_arena --offline
arena-setup --json apply --preset custom \
  --component uci_arena.engine --yes
arena-setup --json verify
.fi
.SH SECURITY
Lichess authentication is a token-file path reference. The Manager and
installer do not open, copy, hash, print, or place token contents in arguments.
Book Forge activation accepts only a typed ready response from its public
retry-auth operation. A reported blocked state receives at most three bounded
attempts; malformed or credential-missing responses fail immediately and the
installer rolls back without printing the token path.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR arena (1)
